  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Should You Refinish or Replace Kitchen Cabinets Before Remodeling?",
    "text": "Should You Refinish or Replace Kitchen Cabinets Before Remodeling?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "Cabinet refinishing is usually a strong option when the cabinet boxes are structurally sound, the layout works, and the main problem is worn or outdated appearance. Replacement becomes more appropriate when cabinets are water-damaged, warped, falling apart, or unable to support the desired layout and storage changes.",
      "@type": "Answer",
